    outlook: "The immediate focus will be on the final stamp of approval from the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI), which is expected shortly. Following this, the NSE will likely commence its roadshows, engaging with institutional investors globally, and announce the crucial price band for the IPO. Investors should closely monitor these developments, along with any further updates on the exact subscription dates and the eventual listing date on competing exchanges like the BSE. The performance of the broader Indian markets will also be a key factor to watch; sustained momentum could lead to an even more enthusiastic reception for the IPO. Any global economic shifts or significant policy announcements from the Indian government could also influence investor sentiment leading up to and immediately after the listing.",
