      bearCase: "The bearish case for Coinbase highlights its continued reliance on volatile retail trading volumes, making it highly susceptible to crypto market downturns. The Q2 revenue miss underscores this vulnerability. For the broader tokenization trend, risks include regulatory fragmentation, cybersecurity threats, and the slow pace of widespread adoption due to complex integration challenges with legacy financial systems.",
      neutralCase: "A neutral perspective suggests a bifurcated market. Retail crypto will remain cyclical and speculative, impacting exchanges like Coinbase. Concurrently, institutional tokenization will continue its methodical, regulated expansion, driven by efficiency gains. These two segments may evolve largely independently, with limited direct spillover in the short term, but converging long-term as underlying DLT infrastructure matures.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "There is a medium probability of continued volatility for retail crypto markets, impacting exchanges. There is a high probability of steady, incremental growth in institutional tokenization and DLT integration into traditional finance, driven by efficiency and regulatory clarity. The long-term outlook for blockchain as a core financial technology is strong, even if retail crypto remains unpredictable.",
